<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-READY-N2>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-READY-N2" ;
  triage:title "ac4_queue_full_offer_is_non_blocking asserts elapsed<1s as its non-blocking proof instead of asserting the actual QueueFull variant/drop counter" ;
  triage:description "fenix reviewer-B (01M1S72R6GNBE5ZETPK6943JMX). crates/atm-observability/src/tracing_bridge.rs:527-536 ac4_queue_full_offer_is_non_blocking asserts `elapsed < 1s` as proof of non-blocking behavior; this is a wall-clock timing assertion, not a behavioral one, and can flake under host contention (false pass on a slow blocking path, false fail on scheduling jitter). Redesign: assert the QueueFull variant and the drop counter directly, no clock; if a did-not-block proof is genuinely needed, run the offer on a thread and recv() a completion signal with no timeout." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
